          "correction": "Run the actual baseline trainer's forward/backward smoke in a supported PyTorch runtime and confirm finite loss and expected encoder/codebook gradients. Keep stability computation export-only; do not invent a dead auxiliary loss."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "integration",
      "verdict": "NEEDS_FIX",
      "findings": [
        {
          "severity": "critical",
          "location": "stage2_RQ-VAE/TIGER_bootstrap_code_stability/train_rqvae.py:110-117,1502-1545",
          "detail": "The submitted tree path contains only PROPOSAL.json, while the claimed implementation is elsewhere under stage2_RQ-VAE/TIGER_bootstrap_code_stability. In that candidate trainer, the data paths are hard-coded to the frozen baseline inputs, but the stability code is not wired into export: the exported .npy/.json remain ordinary collision-extended SIDs, not the required augmented and indexed SIDs. Thus integration and a valid candidate SID export fail. The trainer's existing export indexing enumerates rows, but there is no demonstrated check that the helper's embedding rows and train_ids share this exact item ordering.",
          "reproduction": "Inspect the requested tree at results/research/issue120/trees/round_20261025_021934_521/bootstrap_code_stability: only PROPOSAL.json is present. In the implementation candidate, final export at train_rqvae.py:1537-1544 saves sid and row-enumerated JSON without stability_tokens. The implementation record also acknowledges no valid modified SID export. The environment lacks torch, so the trainer/launcher cannot be run here; launcher code is present at train_rqvae.py:1552-1611 but runtime operation is unverified.",
          "correction": "Place the implementation in the designated candidate tree (or make its location unambiguous), wire train-only statistics and seeded perturbation tokens into the actual final SID export, validate row-to-item alignment against the frozen data mapping and uniqueness/shape/vocabulary constraints, then run the real trainer entry point and distributed launcher under the supported PyTorch environment."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
